Command run on WindowsVM Machine

`for /L %i in (1,1,6) do net use \\127.0.0.1\IPC$ /user:baduser Wrong123`
This command repeated failed logon attempts which is very important in SIEM detection

Possible reasons:
- Brute Force Attack
- Credential Stuffing
- Password Spraying
- Misconfigured System

To reach the event(s)
From the Wazuh Dashboard, click on the NODE that you want to monitor
Click on More, then under Threat Intelligence, select Threat Hunting. 
In the searchbar, type in the ID (i.e. 4625) which will bring up the failed logons

What we should expect in our SIEM
4625 events which are failed logon events and 60122 failed logon rule

With this information, we would be able to set a custom on the Wazuh (SIEM) to escalate repeated failed login requests.



